# The build context is the repository root, and samples/03-modular-data/Dockerfile copies whole
# source trees into it. Without this, a developer's bin/ and obj/ ride along — and a restore
# output carrying Windows absolute paths lands on top of the one the image just produced, which
# fails inside ResolvePackageAssets with a stack trace that says nothing about the cause.
#
# It works on a clean checkout, so CI never saw it. That is the whole reason the image is now
# built by a job rather than by whoever remembers to.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
local-feed/
artifacts/
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
skill/
docs/
tests/
